.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-sound-driver-setup
command detects and enables sound devices by configuring the
system to load the appropriate drivers.

If multiple devices are detected, the user is prompted to change
the default device using auto-select-sound-device(8).

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

